1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,379
The biggest mistake people make

2
00:00:01,379 --> 00:00:03,160
after a painful experience is

3
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,280
trying to get past it

4
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,059
as quickly as possible. Move

5
00:00:06,059 --> 00:00:07,679
on, stay busy, don't think

6
00:00:07,679 --> 00:00:09,019
about it, that sounds healthy,

7
00:00:09,179 --> 00:00:10,740
but it isn't. I spent

8
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:12,439
years treating suffering as a

9
00:00:12,439 --> 00:00:14,140
problem to solve, to get

10
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:15,019
through it, to put it

11
00:00:15,019 --> 00:00:16,539
behind me, to get back

12
00:00:16,539 --> 00:00:17,600
to normal, and I kept

13
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,160
noticing in my own life

14
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:20,539
and in the research that

15
00:00:20,539 --> 00:00:21,679
the people who did that

16
00:00:21,679 --> 00:00:24,160
actually didn't heal faster. They

17
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,039
just stopped feeling, which is

18
00:00:26,039 --> 00:00:27,280
not the same thing. We're

19
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:28,899
wired to avoid pain because

20
00:00:28,899 --> 00:00:30,859
pain signals danger. That was

21
00:00:30,859 --> 00:00:32,840
useful for survival. It's much

22
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,439
less useful for building a

23
00:00:34,439 --> 00:00:36,020
meaningful life because some of

24
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:37,259
the most important things that

25
00:00:37,259 --> 00:00:38,600
will ever happen to you

26
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:40,000
will hurt, and if you

27
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,539
rush past the lesson, you

28
00:00:41,539 --> 00:00:42,799
lose what it was trying

29
00:00:42,799 --> 00:00:44,399
to show you. The Buddhists

30
00:00:44,399 --> 00:00:45,759
have understood this for two

31
00:00:45,759 --> 00:00:46,920
and a half thousand years.

32
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,979
Modern psychology is catching up.

33
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,759
Researchers who study post -traumatic

34
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:52,560
growth keep finding the same

35
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,240
pattern. People who sit with

36
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:55,840
their suffering, who ask what

37
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:57,740
is teaching them, rather than

38
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:59,280
how to escape it, often

39
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:00,679
come out with something the

40
00:01:00,679 --> 00:01:02,399
comfortable life ever gave them.

41
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:05,400
Sharper priorities, deeper relationships, a

42
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,159
clearer sense of what actually

43
00:01:07,159 --> 00:01:08,859
matters. The practice I give

44
00:01:08,859 --> 00:01:10,200
my students is simple. When

45
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,159
something painful happens, don't ask,

46
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,120
how do I get over

47
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:15,079
this? Ask instead, what is

48
00:01:15,079 --> 00:01:16,480
this trying to teach me?

49
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,260
That's a different project, and

50
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:19,519
it's a harder one, but

51
00:01:19,519 --> 00:01:20,500
it's the one that leads

52
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:22,439
somewhere. That question, what is

53
00:01:22,439 --> 00:01:23,540
this trying to show me,

54
00:01:23,579 --> 00:01:25,000
is what the meaning membership

55
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,680
is built around. Every month,

56
00:01:26,799 --> 00:01:27,819
we take one of life's

57
00:01:27,819 --> 00:01:29,680
biggest questions and examine it

58
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,760
together, through research, through ancient

59
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,099
wisdom, and through honest conversation.

60
00:01:34,519 --> 00:01:35,579
Not to arrive at easy

61
00:01:35,579 --> 00:01:37,159
answers, but to become the

62
00:01:37,159 --> 00:01:38,140
kind of people who can

63
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:40,099
hold the real answers. Because

64
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:41,519
meaning isn't something you find

65
00:01:41,519 --> 00:01:43,599
once, it's something that accumulates,

66
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,659
and it accumulates fastest when

67
00:01:45,659 --> 00:01:46,920
you stop running from the

68
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:48,439
things that are trying to

69
00:01:48,439 --> 00:01:49,019
teach you.
